WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.480
If you notice one of the things I said to you.

2
00:00:02.480 --> 00:00:12.200
Early on, through my involvement in 4-H, the agents that I experienced were genuine.

3
00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:17.360
I didn’t wonder if they were helping me because I was African American.

4
00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:22.040
Because they were genuine, they were just helping, they were just teaching.

5
00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:27.160
They were delivering educational information.

6
00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:34.480
Sometimes when you think about social change, some individuals may just do it because they have to.

7
00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:45.720
I’m willing to bet that John Harris, Clay Sampson, Tommy [?], Larry Brock, all them people . . . You know my mom didn’t have anything.

8
00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:48.380
My mom was not a big farmer.

9
00:00:48.380 --> 00:00:54.300
We didn’t have lots of money or anything like that, so they couldn’t have been helping for that reason.

10
00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:55.180
So they had to be genuine.

11
00:00:55.180 --> 00:01:05.920
They had to see something in a little black girl from Clinton that they thought could go forward and become a productive citizen.
